1
00:01:43,630 --> 00:01:47,830
[KING OF COMEDY]

2
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,930
[Episode 9]

3
00:01:51,150 --> 00:01:54,470
I originally gave her a 24K gold one.

4
00:01:54,470 --> 00:01:56,710
Now look, it's turned into a copper one.

5
00:01:56,870 --> 00:01:57,350
Copper?

6
00:01:57,350 --> 00:01:58,080
Impossible.

7
00:01:59,229 --> 00:02:00,510
I didn't switch it.

8
00:02:01,350 --> 00:02:02,510
After you gave it to me,

9
00:02:02,510 --> 00:02:04,920
I returned it to you shortly after.

10
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,680
I didn't switch the ring at all.

11
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,360
How could we have switched the ring?

12
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,310
You two outsiders

13
00:02:10,310 --> 00:02:11,630
are bullying a villager like me,

14
00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:12,310
aren't you?

15
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:14,530
Bullying a widow like me!

16
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,490
I'm telling you,

17
00:02:15,870 --> 00:02:17,190
I can't live like this!

18
00:02:17,190 --> 00:02:18,250
What are you doing?

19
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:21,840
The ground is cold! The ground is cold!

20
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,000
Alright, alright!

21
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,240
Get up!

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,870
Stop arguing!

23
00:02:34,410 --> 00:02:35,400
Just talk about the issue.

24
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:36,400
Don't argue.

25
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:40,470
About what just happened,

26
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:41,750
I roughly understand.

27
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:43,520
You both have your own stories.

28
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:47,420
It's hard for me
to make a judgment right now.

29
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:50,400
But I have an idea.

30
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:53,510
I'll keep the ring for now.

31
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:57,240
I have a cousin who works
at a jewelry store in the city.

32
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,360
I'll have him come here tomorrow.

33
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:01,630
Once he verifies it,

34
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:02,230
we'll know

35
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:04,520
whether it's gold or copper.

36
00:03:05,470 --> 00:03:07,190
If it's copper,

37
00:03:07,710 --> 00:03:10,680
I'll call the police
and have them both arrested.

38
00:03:10,870 --> 00:03:12,870
Chief, you have to stand up for me!

39
00:03:12,870 --> 00:03:14,030
What if it's gold?

40
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:15,710
Trust me.

41
00:03:15,710 --> 00:03:17,840
I will handle this impartially,

42
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:18,400
okay?

43
00:03:21,070 --> 00:03:22,930
Then let's leave it at that, okay?

44
00:03:24,390 --> 00:03:25,590
Everyone, disperse.

45
00:03:25,590 --> 00:03:26,430
Chief, let me tell you.

46
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:29,070
Make her explain clearly! She ran away!

47
00:03:29,070 --> 00:03:31,190
Make her explain it to me clearly!

48
00:03:31,190 --> 00:03:32,430
-She ran away!
-Go home.

49
00:03:32,430 --> 00:03:33,360
She ran away!

50
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,400
Ms. Lin, Ms. Lin!

51
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:35,710
You guys go back first.

52
00:03:35,710 --> 00:03:37,960
I'll personally go to Ms. Haigou's house
to negotiate with her.

53
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:39,750
I absolutely won't let you be wronged!

54
00:03:39,750 --> 00:03:41,210
Okay, we'll go home first.

55
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:42,840
Thank you, Jiahao.

56
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:45,280
I didn't switch it.

57
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,470
It is the one.

58
00:03:46,470 --> 00:03:47,280
Calm down, calm down.

59
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,150
Go talk for me.

60
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:58,010
Ms. Haigou,

61
00:03:58,310 --> 00:04:00,520
I heard your son has been in prison.

62
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:03,120
Don't mention him.

63
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:05,360
He's almost 30.

64
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:06,800
Everyone in the village

65
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:07,600
dislikes him.

66
00:04:07,770 --> 00:04:09,150
Just because he looks fierce,

67
00:04:09,150 --> 00:04:10,590
he can't find a job.

68
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,190
Don't mention it.

69
00:04:13,430 --> 00:04:14,470
Then do me a favor.

70
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:15,840
I'll ask my boss

71
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:17,750
to arrange for your son
to work at our company,

72
00:04:17,750 --> 00:04:18,630
with full benefits.

73
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:19,490
How about that?

74
00:04:20,070 --> 00:04:21,870
T-That would be great!

75
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:23,320
Thank you. Thank you.

76
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:24,140
I... I...

77
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:29,160
T-These Haigou Pills...

78
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,390
My Haigou Pills

79
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:33,390
are all hand-rolled.

80
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:34,540
I... I...

81
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:36,070
I'll give them all to you.

82
00:04:36,070 --> 00:04:36,830
Okay.

83
00:04:36,830 --> 00:04:37,510
These...

84
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:38,830
They're free. They're free.

85
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:39,870
I do need them,

86
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:41,730
but what I need more

87
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:43,050
is this.

88
00:04:50,510 --> 00:04:52,040
You're such a handful.

89
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,730
What can you even do?

90
00:04:56,150 --> 00:04:57,000
Why?

91
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,150
We finally got to this point,

92
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:00,680
and everything was going smoothly.

93
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:02,240
But you wanted a small bargain.

94
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:03,390
If you hadn't accepted it then,

95
00:05:03,390 --> 00:05:04,870
would any of this have happened?

96
00:05:04,870 --> 00:05:05,480
Without this matter,

97
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,070
would you have fallen into a trap?

98
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:08,070
If you had known earlier—

99
00:05:08,070 --> 00:05:09,560
Give it a rest.

100
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,930
Ximei didn't know either.

101
00:05:10,930 --> 00:05:12,000
Besides, where were you earlier?

102
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:12,950
Why didn't you keep an eye on things?

103
00:05:12,950 --> 00:05:13,830
Now that something happened,

104
00:05:13,830 --> 00:05:15,560
you're just nagging.

105
00:05:15,830 --> 00:05:16,870
Why are you blaming me?

106
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:17,680
Why can't I blame you?

107
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:18,510
Can't I blame you?

108
00:05:18,510 --> 00:05:19,270
Zhen, don't...

109
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:19,950
Ximei... Ximei...

110
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:21,600
Don't blame him.

111
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:23,800
It really is my fault.

112
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:25,680
It's okay.

113
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:30,480
I didn't know Ms. Haigou
was that kind of person.

114
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:32,870
The ring is fake.

115
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,680
It's okay.

116
00:05:35,430 --> 00:05:36,390
It's okay.

117
00:05:36,390 --> 00:05:37,270
It's okay. It's okay.

118
00:05:37,270 --> 00:05:38,480
Alright, alright.

119
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,000
It's all your fault.

120
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,130
It's not your fault.

121
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:42,720
Cheek to cheek. It's okay.

122
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:43,720
It's not your fault.

123
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,480
I'm sorry.

124
00:05:49,070 --> 00:05:50,240
It's okay. It's okay.

125
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,440
It's okay. It's okay.

126
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:53,450
Well, is Ms. Haigou

127
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:55,510
always like this?

128
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,680
Her reputation has always been bad,

129
00:05:57,860 --> 00:06:00,590
but I didn't expect her
to do something like that.

130
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,040
My brother has already
gone to talk to them.

131
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,830
I think there must be a way.

132
00:06:04,260 --> 00:06:06,590
Your brother? You really know who to send.

133
00:06:09,510 --> 00:06:10,160
Brother.

134
00:06:13,950 --> 00:06:15,920
As the future village chief,

135
00:06:16,950 --> 00:06:18,560
I went to talk to Ms. Haigou.

136
00:06:20,150 --> 00:06:21,510
But her son, Ma Dajun...

137
00:06:22,190 --> 00:06:23,040
He hit you?

138
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:25,190
No.

139
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:29,310
I looked at him and got scared.

140
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:34,150
I rolled down the stairs!

141
00:06:38,270 --> 00:06:40,480
It's okay.

142
00:06:41,630 --> 00:06:42,190
Well,

143
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:43,830
how is your face okay?

144
00:06:45,870 --> 00:06:47,360
You tell me, how fast

145
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:49,250
can a person's reaction be?

146
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:51,480
When I rolled down, I subconsciously

147
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:53,409
protected my most important part.

148
00:06:53,409 --> 00:06:55,170
So my face wasn't injured.

149
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,150
Pretty smart.

150
00:06:56,630 --> 00:06:59,190
But I hit the back of my head!

151
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:05,190
I even bounced twice!

152
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:07,890
Alright.

153
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:10,040
Stop crying.

154
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:13,720
Crying won't solve the problem.

155
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:16,430
I don't think it's that simple.

156
00:07:16,430 --> 00:07:17,160
Tell me.

157
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:19,800
Ms. Haigou has no grudge against us.

158
00:07:19,830 --> 00:07:21,090
Why would she frame us?

159
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:23,310
Chen Junnan.

160
00:07:24,430 --> 00:07:26,030
That Toothbrush Moustache?

161
00:07:28,750 --> 00:07:29,870
And to think...

162
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:36,190
I saved his life!

163
00:07:37,430 --> 00:07:40,800
I'm going to make him pay
with his life right now!

164
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,240
Come back!

165
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:43,950
I haven't gone far.

166
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:44,600
Sit down.

167
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:46,360
Sit down first.

168
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:48,730
Don't cause any more trouble.

169
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:52,900
I don't think it's him.

170
00:07:53,430 --> 00:07:54,000
This time,

171
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,400
it doesn't seem like something
he's smart enough to pull off.

172
00:07:58,150 --> 00:07:59,630
Then who could it be?

173
00:08:01,870 --> 00:08:05,430
Is there someone else?

174
00:08:06,490 --> 00:08:08,070
Jiaoqi, today was so satisfying.

175
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,120
Look at the village committee.

176
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,600
They had no idea what to do.

177
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:11,160
Pour it.

178
00:08:14,390 --> 00:08:15,990
Pouring it for me from yours?

179
00:08:16,050 --> 00:08:17,850
I... I poured too much into mine.

180
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,560
Where did you get the red wine?

181
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:22,020
From Chen Junnan's store.

182
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:24,040
He...

183
00:08:24,570 --> 00:08:25,670
This doesn't even have alcohol.

184
00:08:25,670 --> 00:08:26,670
It's grape juice.

185
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:28,650
It's a waste to put it in this glass.

186
00:08:32,669 --> 00:08:34,510
The moment they accepted the ring,

187
00:08:34,510 --> 00:08:35,799
we had them trapped.

188
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:39,150
But Jiaoqi, there's one thing
I don't understand.

189
00:08:39,150 --> 00:08:40,750
What if they

190
00:08:40,750 --> 00:08:42,080
don't return the ring

191
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,240
and let Ma Dajun act?

192
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:44,520
What should we do then?

193
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,670
Ma Dajun looks fierce

194
00:08:47,670 --> 00:08:48,510
and can't act.

195
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:51,080
He'll definitely turn
the crew upside down,

196
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:52,840
and the footage will be unwatchable.

197
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,370
They'll shoot for nothing.

198
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,510
Brilliant.

199
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,590
Jiaoqi, this is also
from the Three Kingdoms?

200
00:08:59,590 --> 00:09:00,960
Have you seen "Huarong Road"?

201
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:01,820
I've played it.

202
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:03,640
It's called blocking both ends.

203
00:09:06,990 --> 00:09:08,750
Jiaoqi, you're amazing.

204
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,790
No wonder you can handle my sister

205
00:09:10,790 --> 00:09:11,870
who is so dramatic.

206
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:13,600
Your sister isn't dramatic.

207
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:14,520
She's cute.

208
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:17,900
Your sister... Let's talk about business.

209
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,270
So what's our next plan?

210
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:23,090
I have another plan.

211
00:09:24,670 --> 00:09:25,270
Show-off.

212
00:09:27,910 --> 00:09:29,120
At the end of the day,

213
00:09:29,390 --> 00:09:30,520
it's still my fault.

214
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:32,920
Why couldn't I keep my hands to myself?

215
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,150
You're all here.

216
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:36,280
It'd be a waste to tear down this house.

217
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,030
Close the door!

218
00:09:41,550 --> 00:09:43,210
Open the door. We need to talk.

219
00:09:44,030 --> 00:09:46,430
We have a solution
for Ms. Haigou's matter.

220
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:50,050
-Open the door!
-Open the door!

221
00:09:50,910 --> 00:09:51,360
Speak.

222
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:53,080
Still playing this game.

223
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:54,540
Just stand there and talk.

224
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:55,570
Right there.

225
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:59,000
These sneaky things you've done

226
00:09:59,630 --> 00:10:00,360
are too terrible.

227
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:00,720
Yes.

228
00:10:01,030 --> 00:10:01,840
Too terrible.

229
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:03,480
Worse than the two of us.

230
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:04,750
Wicked.

231
00:10:04,910 --> 00:10:06,960
The villagers' trust in you

232
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:08,560
has dropped significantly.

233
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:09,870
The movie definitely can't be shot.

234
00:10:09,870 --> 00:10:10,360
Yes.

235
00:10:11,390 --> 00:10:12,080
Why don't

236
00:10:12,910 --> 00:10:15,240
you take the lead
in tearing down the house

237
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:18,240
and seek some real benefits
for the villagers?

238
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,510
Close the door!

239
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:20,310
You...

240
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:24,130
How could you...

241
00:10:24,570 --> 00:10:25,900
I have something to say.

242
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,700
Seeking real benefits

243
00:10:34,430 --> 00:10:37,760
means bringing sustainable development
to the villagers,

244
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,670
instead of killing the goose
that lays the golden eggs

245
00:10:41,670 --> 00:10:42,690
and exhausting
the pond to catch all the fish.

246
00:10:42,690 --> 00:10:43,720
Draining the pond to catch all the fish.

247
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:44,600
Draining...

248
00:10:45,390 --> 00:10:47,590
Draining the pond to catch all the fish.

249
00:10:48,150 --> 00:10:50,000
From my father's handwritten book,

250
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,720
page 47, line 3.

251
00:10:53,020 --> 00:10:53,630
Well said!

252
00:10:55,260 --> 00:10:56,660
I don't even understand.

253
00:10:57,750 --> 00:10:58,360
Okay.

254
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:01,090
Let's do as the handwritten book says.

255
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,360
Wish you success.

256
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,020
Wish you good luck.

257
00:11:04,550 --> 00:11:05,080
The ring.

258
00:11:05,910 --> 00:11:07,570
It's the same as Ms. Haigou's.

259
00:11:08,790 --> 00:11:10,120
This is my wedding ring.

260
00:11:10,510 --> 00:11:11,510
Then what are you wearing here?

261
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:12,910
It's my second marriage.

262
00:11:14,670 --> 00:11:16,400
Anyway, make a decision early.

263
00:11:17,080 --> 00:11:19,510
If you're late, even the electric bikes
will be gone.

264
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:20,870
Close the door!

265
00:11:20,870 --> 00:11:22,150
The ring. The ring.

266
00:11:23,870 --> 00:11:24,930
The ring. The ring.

267
00:11:25,670 --> 00:11:26,320
Reckless.

268
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,530
J-Jiaoqi, don't go yet.

269
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:32,900
You just said you were married twice.

270
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:35,080
Is my sister the first or the second?

271
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,080
What do you think?

272
00:11:36,390 --> 00:11:38,050
Isn't this Ms. Haigou's ring?

273
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,030
Are you sure?

274
00:11:39,030 --> 00:11:40,230
Very sure. Very sure.

275
00:11:40,790 --> 00:11:41,520
Case closed.

276
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,490
Let me pour you some.

277
00:11:50,870 --> 00:11:51,480
Again?

278
00:11:57,480 --> 00:11:58,510
Why is it you?

279
00:11:59,630 --> 00:12:00,680
It's okay, Ximei.

280
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:03,160
I don't blame you.

281
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:04,510
Whether you blame me or not,

282
00:12:04,510 --> 00:12:06,370
I didn't splash the wrong person.

283
00:12:06,390 --> 00:12:07,600
You are all in this together.

284
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:09,130
None of you are good people.

285
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:10,630
Your master has already left.

286
00:12:10,630 --> 00:12:11,270
You're late.

287
